The changes I made include:

1. Added the AppProvider wrapper which is required for the AppCard component to work properly
2. Added missing properties to the app object:
   - categories: Added as an array with "payment" category
   - isInstalled: Set to true
   - enabled: Set to true
   - isSetupAlready: Set to true
3. These properties are required by the AppCard component and were causing the error when trying to access categories[0]

The error was occurring because the app object didn't have the categories array, which is required by the AppCard component. The AppCard component tries to access the first category with `categories[0]`, which was causing the "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading '0')" error.

This solution should resolve the error while maintaining the functionality of the component. The AppProvider context is also necessary for the component to work properly as it provides necessary context values used by the AppCard component.

